 ## Operating characteristics
 *   **Time Complexity**: $O(N_{\text{cells}} \cdot N_{\text{triangles}})$ per voxelization pass, where $N_{\text{cells}}$ is the number of voxels and $N_{\text{triangles}}$ is the number of triangles in the mesh. This is brute-force and does not use spatial acceleration structures [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity**: $O(N_{\text{cells}})$ for the output grid, plus $O(N_{\text{vertices}} + N_{\text{indices}})$ for the input mesh buffers [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths**: Simple implementation; no complex spatial data structures required; parallelizable across voxels [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations**: Performance degrades linearly with mesh complexity and grid resolution; unsuitable for very high-poly meshes or large grids without optimization [S1, unofficial].
